      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the sum of all the positive divisors of 91, we first need to determine its prime factorization. \n\n91 can be factored as 7 x 13, since 7 x 13 = 91.\n\nNow, we can use the formula for finding the sum of divisors:\n\nSum of divisors = (p1^(a1+1) - 1)/(p1 - 1) * (p2^(a2+1) - 1)/(p2 - 1) * ... * (pk^(ak+1) - 1)/(pk - 1)\n\nwhere p1, p2, ..., pk are the prime factors of the number, and a1, a2, ..., ak are their respective exponents.\n\nIn this case, p1 = 7, a1 = 1, p2 = 13, and a2 = 1.\n\nSo, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is:\n\n(7^(1+1) - 1)/(7 - 1) * (13^(1+1) - 1)/(13 - 1)\n= (7^2 - 1)/(7 - 1) * (13^2 - 1)/(13 - 1)\n= (49 - 1)/6 * (169 - 1)/12\n= 48/6 * 168/12\n= 8 * 14\n= 112\n\nSo, the sum of all the positive divisors of 91 is 112.",
